                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.07392/2611.07392v1/wgov3_beta_attention_mask_cot_square_matrix.png",
                "caption": "Figure 4:Block-structured attention mask for a generation sequence containing\nprompt text, a condition image, CoT text, and a noisy target. Rows denote\nqueries and columns denote keys/values; gray cells are visible and white cells\nare masked. Text blocks use causal attention, whereas the condition image and\nnoisy target use bidirectional attention within their respective blocks.\nEach block can attend to preceding conditions, while noisy-target keys/values\nremain hidden from earlier blocks. Purple marks CoT tokens receiving\ncross-entropy supervision, and the inset shows isolation between packed\nsamples.",
                "position": 995
            }
